        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-116" edge="1" parent="1" source="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-117" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-119" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-117" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Web Servers" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="69.26" width="125" x="2015" y="3247.74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-118" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;" value="Cache" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="1875" y="3376" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-119" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;" value="DatBase" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="2128" y="3376" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-120" edge="1" parent="1" source="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-121" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-122" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-121" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Method 3&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Generating Keys Offline&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;We can have a standalone Key Generation Service (KGS) that generates random seven letter strings&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;beforehand and stores them in a database (let’s call it key-DB). Whenever we want to shorten a URL,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;we will just take one of the already-generated keys and use it. This approach will make things quite&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;simple and fast. Not only are we not encoding the URL, but we won’t have to worry about duplications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;or collisions. KGS will make sure all the keys inserted into key-DB are unique&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Concurrency ? - &lt;/b&gt;As soon as key is used it will marked in the DB to ensure it will not be used again&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 16px; margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;How to solve when two sever try to read the same key&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Servers can use KGS to read/mark keys in the database. KGS can use two tables to store keys: one for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;keys that are not used yet, and one for all the used keys. As soon as KGS gives keys to one of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;servers, it can move them to the used keys table. KGS can always keep some keys in memory so that it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;can quickly provide them whenever a server needs them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;For simplicity, as soon as KGS loads some keys in memory, it can move them to the used keys table.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;This ensures each server gets unique keys. If KGS dies before assigning all the loaded keys to some&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;server, we will be wasting those keys–which is acceptable, due to large numbers of keys we have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;KGS also has to make sure not to give the same key to multiple servers. For that, it must synchronize&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;(or get a lock on) the data structure holding the keys before removing keys from it and giving them to a&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;What would be the key-DB size?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;With 62^7 ~ 35.21B keys (1Byte - one alpha-numeric character)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;7*(35.21B) ~ 246GB&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KGS a single point failure?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Yes, it is. To solve this, we can have a standby replica of KGS.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Whenever the primary server dies, the standby server can take over to generate and provide keys.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="609" width="623.5" x="289.5" y="3505" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-122" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;" value="&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data Partitioning and Replication&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;To scale out our DB, we need to partition it so that it can store information about billions of URLs&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;- Range Based Partitioning: We can store the URL by there first letter of URL or HashKey&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;Problem with this approach is that it can lead up to unbalanced server&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;- Hash Based Partitioning :&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;In hash-based partitioning, we apply a hash function on a key (e.g., short URL key or original URL) and use the hash value to decide which partition stores the data. For example, a hash function may map a key to a number between &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;391&quot; data-end=&quot;400&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;1–256&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, where each number represents a partition. This helps distribute data evenly and enables fast lookups, since the same key always maps to the same partition.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;559&quot; data-end=&quot;802&quot;&gt;However, uneven traffic or hot keys can still overload certain partitions. To handle this, &lt;strong data-start=&quot;650&quot; data-end=&quot;672&quot;&gt;consistent hashing&lt;/strong&gt; is used,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Load Balancer&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;We can add a Load balancing layer at three places in our system:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;1. Between Clients and Application servers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;2. Between Application Servers and database servers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;3. Between Application Servers and Cache servers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Purging and DB clean UP&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="369.75" width="468" x="981" y="3624.63" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-123" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="357" width="693.36" x="1473.5" y="3641" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p-asIFV21MIEWjqzHZch-124" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;" value="ff" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="4381" width="2472" x="40" y="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
